> Retain the original sixteen-vertex graph and native stream

The native graph helper preserves the original xorshift64 seed999 construction:
inspect upper-triangle pairs, include an edge on an odd draw, then draw its
integer weight1..9. Both adjacency directions retain original insertion order.
The original solver request uses population24,40 offspring generations and
seed1. Its13/7/17 unsigned xorshift, modulo tournament choices, crossover bits,
top53-bit mutation uniforms and zero-seed fallback retain the original stream
conventions, including modulo bias.

The next program obtains the entire actual generation0..40 history from one
native run. It does not rerun truncated independent optimizations to manufacture
a trajectory. A separate native full-enumeration helper fixes vertex0 side0,
exploiting complement symmetry, and checks every remaining partition on this
small graph. Equality with that exact comparator supports this one fixture, not
a general guarantee. A history can be flat if initialization already finds a
strong candidate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/memetic_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto graph = dm::algorithms::memetic_demo_graph();
    auto t = dm::algorithms::memetic_max_cut_trace(16, graph, 24, 40, 1);
    auto exact = dm::algorithms::memetic_max_cut_exact(16, graph);
    std::print("Actual completed request {}; actual best {:.0f}; complete-enumeration optimum {:.0f}; " "actual evaluated candidates {}; actual RNG draws {}; actual local checks {}.\n\n| actual " "installed generation | actual population best | actual mean fitness | actual distinct cuts " "modulo complement |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               t.analysis.complete, t.analysis.result.value, exact.value,
               t.analysis.work.individuals, t.analysis.work.rng_draws,
               t.analysis.work.local_checks);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (auto &g : t.generations) {
        std::print("| {} | {:.0f} | {:.8f} | {} |\n", g.index, g.best_value,
                   g.mean_fitness, g.distinct_cuts);
        x.push_back(g.index);
        y.push_back(g.best_value);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual population best", {37, 99, 235});
    p.points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235});
    p.legend({"actual population best", "enumerated optimum"},
             {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}});
    p.abline_h(exact.value, {220, 38, 38}, 1.5).x_label("actual installed generation, initialization0").y_label("actual weighted cut objective").title("Original graph: one actual native population trajectory").save_svg("build/memetic_original.svg");
}
```
