The actual initialization already attains the enumerated optimum195 on this
fixture, and its best value stays195 through all40 offspring generations. The
flat curve records that observation rather than an improvement caused by later
generations.

> Population diversity is an observation

A partition and its complete bit complement represent the same cut. The native
generation snapshot therefore counts distinct cuts after identifying those
complements, alongside the actual mean fitness. This summary is computed from
the installed population and does not change solver RNG draws or selected
algorithm counters. It measures this run’s diversity; it is not a bound on
search quality or a proof that more distinct candidates improve the objective.

The next program reads another reproducible native run with the same original
request and plots its actual installed-population diversity. Its identical
seed/model reproduces the previous trajectory rather than adding independent
replications or uncertainty intervals.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/memetic_diversity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::memetic_max_cut_trace(16,
                                              dm::algorithms::memetic_demo_graph(),
                                              24, 40, 1);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual installed generation | actual distinct cuts modulo complement | actual mean " "fitness | actual selected best |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &g : t.generations) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.8f} | {:.0f} |\n", g.index, g.distinct_cuts,
                   g.mean_fitness, g.best_value);
        x.push_back(g.index);
        y.push_back(g.distinct_cuts);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual distinct cuts", {37, 99, 235});
    p.points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235});
    p.legend({"actual distinct cuts"}, {{37, 99, 235}});
    p.y_limits(0, 25).x_label("actual installed generation").y_label(
        "actual distinct cuts among24 members").title("Original run: measured population diversity").save_svg("build/memetic_diversity.svg");
}
```
