> Input, numeric and bounded-work contracts

The checked graph has exactly N ordered weighted lists. Every neighbour id is
valid, weights are finite and each directed entry has an equal-weight reverse
entry with matching multiplicity. Parallel edges are allowed and summed
separately; self loops are rejected because the flip-gain formula would
otherwise count them incorrectly. Signed finite weights are allowed. Original
row order is preserved for floating sums. Complete absolute undirected weight
range and actual objective/delta computations must remain finite;
unrepresentable geometry and malformed populations/generations throw before
evaluation. Every evaluated partition is binary and has exactly N entries.

Requested population size is positive, generations nonnegative. Runtime stores
O(PN) population bits plus graph/validation and candidate state. Work depends on
actual local checks and incident-row reads; no polynomial global-search or
universal local-sweep bound is claimed. Empty graphs and population-one runs
retain their actual native lifecycle. Complete=true means the requested
initialization/generations finished, not that a global optimum was proved.
locally_refined means the winning candidate completed its computed1e−12 no-flip
terminal sweep.

An optional global local-check cap, zero unlimited, stops before the next vertex
delta. The producer evaluates the actual partially refined candidate and returns
complete=false with the best actually evaluated valid partition. Its winner can
be marked not locally refined. Validation, random draws, objective evaluation
and wall time are outside this selected-operation cap. Unfinished generations do
not appear as installed snapshots.

Complete logical capture starts with5+2N+2E_list entries: five scalar run
inputs, original graph vertex slots, neighbour-id/weight scalars and returned
best bits. Add every actual RNG/local record, each candidate record and its two
N-bit endpoint snapshots, and each installed generation record with PN
population bits and P fitness values. Default cap one million; zero disables it.
Fields, row headers, capacities, runtime/returned duplicate copies and bytes are
excluded. Actual capture contributions are admitted before owned copies. A work
stop returns complete actual bounded history; a capture failure throws without a
prefix.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/memetic_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::MemeticGraph graph{{{1, 1}, {2, 1}}, {{0, 1}, {2, 1}},
                                       {{0, 1}, {1, 1}}};
    auto exact = dm::algorithms::memetic_max_cut_exact(3, graph);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| prescribed local-check cap | actual local checks | complete requested run | best locally " "refined | initialized population | installed offspring generations | actual best objective " "| actual capture entries |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t cap : {1, 3, 12, 24, 48, 96}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::memetic_max_cut_trace(3, graph, 4, 2, 1, cap);
        auto &a = t.analysis;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", cap,
                   a.work.local_checks, a.complete, a.locally_refined,
                   a.initialized, a.generations_completed, a.result.value,
                   t.captured_entries);
        x.push_back(cap);
        y.push_back(a.result.value);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual best evaluated cut", {37, 99, 235});
    p.points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235});
    p.legend({"actual best evaluated cut", "enumerated optimum"},
             {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}});
    p.abline_h(exact.value, {220, 38, 38}, 1.5).x_label("prescribed actual local-check cap").y_label("actual feasible cut objective").title("Triangle: bounded work and honest request status").save_svg("build/memetic_controls.svg");
}
```
